  abstract = {10-40\% of bird and mammal spp require cavities for nesting and roosting - tree-cavity supply can be limiting. In North America, avian excavators are the primary cavity producers, but not elsewhere. There is low persistence of woodpecker-excavated cavities in poland and argentina versus Canada. Outside of North America, most cavity-using vertebrates depend on the slow formation of cavities by damage and decay. Therefore, the communities that depend on cavities rely on changing forest policies to stem the current loss of old trees.},
